{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791596850,"nonce":"DkQKGnKSxoZp8yv6we0FJVppcK0=","message":"Plan (2026-10-10). blinc_abi 806be9c has parsing, the cascade, layout writes and typed paint writes; css::styled::Styles runs over an owned LayoutContext only.\n\n**Shape**\nReplace what ashui's Css.restyle computes, which rules match and what each element's values and resolved declarations are, with the native cascade. Keep the Haxe apply layer, Properties.apply through node.styleAll with its fields, transitions, animations and pointer queries, fed from the native resolved declarations. Moving the apply layer to native paint and layout writes is later work, done only where no motion depends on Haxe applying.\n\n**Phase 1, blinc_abi**\n- Styles over a host trait (parent, children, live, apply layout), so it runs over the HashLink Tree as well as a LayoutContext. On HashLink it does not apply layout itself; it reports which nodes' resolved declarations changed.\n- HashLink primitives: a Styles per tree; add a sheet from text (with diagnostics) or compiled bytes; remove; theme variables; media environment and root font size; describe an element (types, id, classes, attributes, inline declarations, anonymous); states; moved, children_changed, forget; restyle; read a node's resolved declarations and computed values.\n\n**Phase 2, ashui**\n- Behind a define first: Identity describes elements to native, tree edits mark moves, Interaction pushes states, the theme and viewport go across, and Css.restyle takes resolved declarations from native.\n- Parity: the CSS tests and every pixel probe, under both engines. Then make native the default and delete the Haxe matcher and cascade.\n\n**Phase 3**\nKeyframes, Css.select and stylesheet introspection read from native (css::json), and CssParser goes.\n\n**Phase 4**\nCompiledCss through the blinc-css tool: diagnostics as compile errors at their line, bytes embedded with Context.addResource.\n\n**Phase 5**\nStartup and restyle measured against the Haxe engine; no slower.","files":null}]}